  "id": "briar-glen-lane",
  "name": "Briar Glen: the shop lane",
  "description": "Bead mw-ju8.5: a greybox cobbled lane, about 40 m long and 16 m wide, built from the e00 kit only. It runs north from the town end of the Miners' Bridge (the bridge-town-end marker; the bridge-gate transition just south of it leads back to valley-03). Marsh's General Store is the first building past the bridge, on the west side: its front door (marsh-store-door) is a transition into the shop (mw-e01.11). Arrival spawns arrive-from-valley-03, arrive-from-marsh-store and arrive-from-sleeping-ox are where the player stands when coming from those scenes; the inn has no door here yet (mw-ju8.22), so arrive-from-sleeping-ox is a marker for it. On the east side three open-fronted shops stand side by side, each with a six metre counter and its keeper behind it: Brand's Forge (Oswin Brand; anvil, forge fire, weapon rack, quench barrel), Fenn's Fletchery & Simples (Juniper Fenn; bow rack, herb bench, arrow barrel) and Pell's Bakery (Hollis Pell; bread shelf, oven, flour sacks). Each counter is a spawn tagged merchant:<id> with the Trade verb and dev-crowns:400 so the dev scene can trade. Props are kit stand-ins with named marker spawns so art can dress them later; street and shop lanterns are warm. Reach it with ?scene=briar-glen-lane.",
